      "questions": {
        "addressed": {
          "type": "choice",
          "instructions": "Is the specific requirement of `anchor.statement` present in `item.text`? The requirement is that sc-agent writes each session row to the repository's SQLite database through sc-agent-sqlite, and no code writes sessions.jsonl. Examples of presence: 'session rows are inserted through sc-agent-sqlite into the repository database', 'sessions.jsonl is no longer written'. Being about the same area, or doing the opposite, is not presence. A bare mention of the topic, or a plan to work on it, without the specific content is no, not unclear. Reading session rows through sc-agent-sqlite, or importing old sessions.jsonl files through it, counts as presence. An item that still writes sessions.jsonl does not carry the requirement.",
          "criteria": {
            "yes": "The requirement is present in the item text, in any wording.",
            "no": "The requirement is absent from the item text.",
            "unclear": "Something resembling the requirement appears, but whether it is the requirement cannot be determined."
          }
        },
        "contradicted": {
          "type": "choice",
          "instructions": "Does `item.text` plan something that breaks `anchor.statement` (sc-agent writes each session row to the repository's SQLite database through sc-agent-sqlite, and no code writes sessions.jsonl)? Breaking it means, for example: writing or appending session rows to sessions.jsonl or another file, or writing session rows to SQLite without going through sc-agent-sqlite. Silence about the requirement is not a conflict, and an item that merely does not mention it answers no. Judge conflict only.",
          "criteria": {
            "yes": "The item plans something that breaks the requirement, for example: writing or appending session rows to sessions.jsonl or another file, or writing session rows to SQLite without going through sc-agent-sqlite.",
            "no": "Nothing in the item breaks the requirement, whether or not the item mentions it.",
            "unclear": "The item plans something that might break the requirement, but the text does not settle it."
          }
        },
        "relevant": {
          "type": "choice",
          "instructions": "`anchor.scope` names the work this anchor governs: code that writes or reads session rows. Decide whether the planning item in `item.text` plans or changes that work, directly or as a stated prerequisite. Do not judge compliance or conflict. An item that only documents, describes, reviews or plans this subject still touches it.",
          "criteria": {
            "yes": "The item plans or changes code that writes or reads session rows.",
            "no": "The item plans other work; code that writes or reads session rows is not part of it.",
            "unclear": "It cannot be told from the item text what part of the system it changes."
          }
        }
      }
    },
